    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for decitabine is present in the supplied records.",
    "No decitabine-specific Caco-2/PAMPA, transporter, efflux, or intestinal metabolism data are available.",
    "No data on cytidine deaminase-mediated first-pass metabolism or acid stability of the 5-aza-triazinone ring are supplied.",
    "BCRP efflux evidence is for cladribine, not decitabine, and active-transport evidence is for gemcitabine/cladribine/NHC, not decitabine.",
    "The threshold-relevant low prediction would require transferable direct low outcomes or decitabine-specific efflux/metabolism evidence, which are absent."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high because L5 provides transporter-mediated uptake evidence for close deoxycytidine/nucleoside analogs and shows that low Caco-2 permeability does not preclude high oral bioavailability (EFdA), undermining the L4 low-permeability basis; no decitabine-specific low F or efflux/metabolism evidence is supplied. Confidence is low because all decisive evidence is indirect."
}

